<speak>She is. She will say, very cheerfully, that lunch conversation is lunch conversation until someone puts an appointment into the diary. My brother was a little offended the first time, but now he repeats the line himself. I think he enjoys having a phrase for it. We have also stopped using the family chat for ordinary office arrangements. Otherwise a photograph of someone's dinner would sit between a meeting message and a reminder about a visitor, and nobody could find anything.</speak>